  "text": "ZEMA invites comments on the Mimbula Phase 3 Expansion Project\n\nThe Zambia Environmental Management Agency (ZEMA) has received an Environmental Impact Statement for the Mimbula Phase 3 Expansion Project in Chingola district, Copperbelt Province. The developer, Mimbula Minerals Limited, submitted the Environmental Impact Statement on 14 September 2026.\n\nThe project will add a new open pit and a heap leach pad to the Mimbula copper mine. It will raise cathode output to 30,000 tonnes a year. The developer estimates the capital cost at US$120 million.\n\nPublic consultation meetings will take place in Chingola on 1 October 2026. Written comments must reach ZEMA by 16 October 2026.",
